  Population & Housing Census 2022:
  1.
  Key Demographic and Socio-Economic Indicators
  1.0 Introduction
  Statistics Botswana conducted a Population and Housing Census in March 2022 after an initial delay
  due to the onset of the COVID 19 which resulted in restricted population movement. Following
  the conclusion of the field enumeration, Statistics Botswana released preliminary results in May of
  2022, followed by Population of Cities and Towns, Population of Villages and Localities report. These
  products ensured that Statistics Botswana continued to discharge its mandate of providing official
  statistics to inform important decision making. An immediate use of the above products was to inform
  the process of constituency delimitation, the budgeting process, formulation of a national transitional
  development plan among others.
  It is important to highlight that given the growth in demand for shortened periodicity to avail data
  for decision making, it is important for Statistics Botswana to embrace innovative methods of data
  collection and processing. In this connection, this was the first digital census from cartographic
  work to use of digital devices for data collection. Statistics Botswana only stands to learn from some
  challenges encountered during implementation of a digital census and such lessons will be extended
  to household surveys as well as other data collection platforms.
  This Census Stats brief presents highlights on a selection of key indicators which have been prioritised
  for release. The results are given in table 1 below with brief discussion in the subsequent paragraphs.
  It must be noted that, a more extensive and detailed analyses of the below highlights, will be given
  in an analytical report to be released in after the census analytical papers dissemination conference
  next year.
  Statistics Botswana
